course: dictionary
lesson: 9390
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Spring is a good example. It can be a season, a coil of metal, a place where water comes up out of the ground, or a way of saying to jump quickly.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Birds may nest in a nest box in spring» tells you spring is a time of year, because birds nest in a season. «The cat sprang onto the wall» has the verb sprang, which is the past of spring, and it means jumped quickly.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. A season fits «in spring», a jump fits «sprang onto the wall», and a coil fits a spring in a pen. If your meaning sounds silly, try another one, just as you would with any new word.
explain: Spring also appears in phrases. «Spring-cleaning» is a big clean of the house, often done in spring, and «spring up» means to appear suddenly. Phrases are groups of words that carry a meaning together, so read the whole group, not just one word.
fact: A word can have several meanings, and the context shows which one is right.
fact: Spring can be a season of three months, between winter and summer, when plants start to grow.
fact: A spring is a coil of metal that goes back to its shape after you press or pull it, like the spring in a pen.
fact: A spring is also a place where water comes up out of the ground, and some rivers start from one.
fact: To spring means to jump quickly, as in «the cat sprang onto the wall».
exercise: «Birds may nest in a nest box in spring.» What does spring mean here? | To jump quickly | *A season of three months, between winter and summer | A coil of metal that goes back to its shape | A place where water comes out of the ground
exercise: «The cat sprang onto the wall.» What does sprang mean? | Grew slowly from a seed | *Jumped quickly up | Went under water | Was a season of the year
exercise: The pen clicks back because of a tiny metal part inside. What is a spring in a pen? | To jump quickly | A place where water comes out of the ground | A season of the year | *A coil of metal that goes back to its shape
test: «Some hot springs smell of it too.» What is a spring in this sentence? | To jump quickly | A season of the year | A coil of metal | *A place where water comes up out of the ground
test: A new shop can spring up overnight. What does spring up mean? | To jump onto a wall | To be wound tight like a coil | *To appear suddenly | To grow slowly from a seed
exam: Which sentence uses spring as a verb meaning to jump quickly? | *«The frog will spring over the stone» | «The spring in the bed is broken» | «Lambs in spring fields need care» | «The hot spring was warm»
